  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the city of Oswego, in the county of Oswego to offer an\noptional twenty-year retirement plan to police officer Zackary Quinones",
    "basePrintNo": "S4790",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4790-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4790\n\nSPONSOR: RITCHIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the city of Oswego, in the county\nof Oswego to offer an optional twenty-year retirement plan to police\nofficer Zackary Quinones\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill authorizes the City of Oswego to offer an optional twenty year\nretirement plan to police officer Zackary Quinones, who failed to file\npaperwork to participate in such retirement plan due to no fault of his\nown.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Establishes the authority to transfer service credit.\n\nSection 2: Requires past service costs to be borne by the City of Oswego\nover a 10-year period.\n\nSection 3: Sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor reasons not ascribable to his own negligence, Zackary Quinones\nfailed to make a timely application to participate in the twenty year\nretirement plan established pursuant to section 384-d of the retirement\nand social security law. This legislation would give Zackary Quinones\neighteen months from the effective date of this act to file a request\nwith the state comptroller to be enrolled and covered under such retire-\nment plan.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is new legislation in 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nSee bill text.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
